%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% requires: resident-outlines
% expect-output: true
% Scenario: name lookup in a TrueType asset. Helvetica's H outline is
% found by its post name in Liberation Sans, and its width at size 100
% is within 2 units of the Helvetica AFM's H bounding box width, 56.9.
% The run's start point and the trailing point at the advance lie on
% the baseline and would bracket the outline in pathbbox, so the glyph
% is sheared by its own height: under [100 0 100 100 0 0] the top-right
% corner lands at urx + ury and under [100 0 -100 100 0 0] the top-left
% at llx - ury, and H's stems reach the top, so the two boxes give the
% outline's width.
% Expect: true.
/Helvetica findfont dup
[100 0 100 100 0 0] makefont setfont
0 0 moveto (H) false charpath
pathbbox /ury exch def /urx exch def pop pop
newpath
[100 0 -100 100 0 0] makefont setfont
0 0 moveto (H) false charpath
pathbbox pop pop pop /llx exch def
urx ury sub llx ury add sub 56.9 sub abs 2 le =
